(Executive Summary) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 606 Tm
(Guardian Shell is a Linux security product for AI agents. It uses eBPF to observe agent) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 591 Tm
(behavior at the kernel boundary and can block selected file and command actions.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 566 Tm
(Its core value is not simply "kernel enforcement." Its real value is:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 541 Tm
(- governing a live AI agent session) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 520 Tm
(- applying policy per agent) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 499 Tm
(- tracking subprocesses) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 478 Tm
(- supporting human approvals) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 457 Tm
(- producing usable audit and operational visibility) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 436 Tm
(This makes it different from traditional Linux controls and also different from products) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 421 Tm
(such as Veto.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 396 Tm
(The Short Verdict) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 373 Tm
(Guardian Shell is already a credible foundation for agent governance on Linux.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 348 Tm
(Its strongest qualities are:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 323 Tm
(1. agent-centric identity, especially with cgroups) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 302 Tm
(2. a practical product layer: approvals, dashboard, alerts, metrics, CLI) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 281 Tm
(3. governance across files, commands, and network visibility) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 260 Tm
(4. a realistic path toward stronger enforcement without discarding the product plane) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 239 Tm
(Its biggest current weakness is:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 214 Tm
(1. too much trust still rests on path-based, tracepoint-first policy decisions) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 193 Tm
(The best path forward is:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 168 Tm
(1. keep the current product and control-plane design) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 147 Tm
(2. move core file and exec decisions deeper into LSM-based canonical or inode-aware) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 132 Tm
(   enforcement) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 111 Tm
(3. add seccomp as a standard hardening layer) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 488 44 Tm
(Page 1 of 30) Tj
